<title>FINLAND: FOREIGN OWNERSHIP IN FINNISH COMPANIES UP IN FEB.</title>
<headline>FOREIGN OWNERSHIP IN FINNISH COMPANIES UP IN FEB.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign ownership of Finnish firms registered in the Central Share Register (OKR) rose to 27.7 percent of shares at end-February from 27.2 percent at end-January, OKR said in a review received on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Foreign ownership in telecoms group Nokia was up</p>
<p>to 72.62 percent at end-February from 71.40 percent at</p>
<p>end-January, OKR said.</p>
<p>Foreign holdings in fur auctioner Turkistuottajat </p>
<p>jumped to 19.04 percent from 2.75 percent.</p>
<p>Foreign holdings in compass maker Suunto rose to</p>
<p>25.49 percent from 18.88 percent and foreign holdings in sauna</p>
<p>equipment maker Saunatec rose to 16.95 percent from</p>
<p>13.29 percent.</p>
